{"name":"Old Army Helmet","hex":"#616652","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"old","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mochi."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an object, concept, relationship, etc., having existed for a relatively long period of time.","Of a living being, having lived for most of the expected years."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old"},{"term":"army","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, highly organized military force, concerned mainly with ground (rather than air or naval) operations.","Used absolutely for that entire branch of the armed forces."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/army"},{"term":"helmet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard, protective head covering, typically part of armour.","That which resembles a helmet in form, position, etc.\nThe upper part of a chemist's retort."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with, or as if with, a helmet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/helmet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Army","blocks":[{"text":"An army, ground force or land force is an armed force that fights primarily on land. In the broadest sense, it is the land-based military branch, service branch, or armed service of a nation or country. It may also include aviation assets by possessing an army aviation component. Within a national military force, the word army may also mean a field army."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/250th_United_States_Army_Birthday_Parade_in_Washington%2C_D.C._on_June_14%2C_2025_-_262.jpg/330px-250th_United_States_Army_Birthday_Parade_in_Washington%2C_D.C._on_June_14%2C_2025_-_262.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Army","wikidata":"Q37726"},{"title":"Helmet","blocks":[{"text":"A helmet is a form of protective gear worn to protect the head. More specifically, a helmet complements the skull in protecting the human brain. Ceremonial or symbolic helmets without protective function are sometimes worn. Soldiers wear combat helmets, often made from Kevlar or other lightweight synthetic fibers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_Wide_Variety_Of_Helmets.png/330px-A_Wide_Variety_Of_Helmets.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helmet","wikidata":"Q173603"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/The_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passes_through_the_Rajpath_during_the_65th_Republic_Day_Parade_2014%2C_in_New_Delhi_on_January_26%2C_2014.jpg/500px-The_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passes_through_the_Rajpath_during_the_65th_Republic_Day_Parade_2014%2C_in_New_Delhi_on_January_26%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/The_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passes_through_the_Rajpath_during_the_65th_Republic_Day_Parade_2014%2C_in_New_Delhi_on_January_26%2C_2014.jpg/1280px-The_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passes_through_the_Rajpath_during_the_65th_Republic_Day_Parade_2014%2C_in_New_Delhi_on_January_26%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/The_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passes_through_the_Rajpath_during_the_65th_Republic_Day_Parade_2014%2C_in_New_Delhi_on_January_26%2C_2014.jpg/500px-The_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passes_through_the_Rajpath_during_the_65th_Republic_Day_Parade_2014%2C_in_New_Delhi_on_January_26%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Indian Army soldiers on parade in 2014","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passes_through_the_Raj